### RQ-007: MotherDuck

**Core question**  
What is MotherDuck precisely, and what is it explicitly **not**?

**In scope**  
Official product architecture and relationship to DuckDB.

**Out of scope**  
Pricing, marketing claims of superiority, future features not in current docs.

**Resolution (documented fact, high confidence)**  
MotherDuck is a **serverless cloud analytics service / data warehouse built on DuckDB**. It runs DuckDB under the hood, speaks DuckDB SQL, and adds cloud storage, sharing, hypertenancy (per-user isolated “Duckling” compute instances), Dual Execution (hybrid local + cloud), and collaboration features.

**Boundary sentence**  
> MotherDuck is a serverless cloud service that runs DuckDB as its engine and adds managed storage, sharing, and per-user compute isolation; it is not a reimplementation of the DuckDB query engine itself and does not replace the open-source in-process DuckDB library.

**Falsifier test**  
No evidence that MotherDuck natively reimplements or replaces the core DuckDB engine; official docs repeatedly state it “runs DuckDB” and “is built on DuckDB.” Falsifier does not fire.

**Verdict**: **resolved**  
Sources: motherduck.com/docs/architecture-and-capabilities, motherduck.com product pages, DuckDB library entry on MotherDuck.  
Access date: 2026-09-28

